#
# Two different kinds of settings live here, and they're reported separately
# so a reviewer can tell which is which:
#  - System-wide toggles (DEP, ASLR, SEHOP, heap corruption termination, and
#    CFG on builds that support a system default for it) really do apply to
#    every process, so these get turned on directly via Set-ProcessMitigation.
